  "conversation_comments": [
    {
      "id": "IC_kwDOR7A3_s8AAAABJi83Cg",
      "body": "## Owner review \u2014 round 1: REQUEST CHANGES (one blocker, one required either/or)\n\n**Pinned head:** `f2d1bcb1dd253f9418f635cbf88d820b424347a5` (item-3 design approved pre-implementation; items 1/2 byte-identical to the previously verified `6d07cc239`).\n\n**F1 \u2014 BLOCKER: the process-wide latch silences the lifecycle evidence for every terminal booking-error after the first.**\n`apply_settlement_booking_terminal_release` gates the `SettlementBookingTerminal` lifecycle evidence AND the `log::error!` behind `settlement_booking_terminal_latched` (mod.rs:1260) \u2014 a once-per-process bool. The exposure release, however, applies on every call. Failure scenario: two settlement failures on different markets in one session \u2192 the second position's exposure is released to Flat with **no lifecycle evidence linking that position to its terminal state and no ERROR line** \u2014 a silent Flat, which the approved design's first constraint (\"fail-loud, no silent absorption\") explicitly forbids. The sticky-once semantics belong to the *operator signal* only; the lifecycle evidence was specified per terminal event.\n**Fix:** dedupe the lifecycle evidence + ERROR per settlement key (mirroring the existing booking-error evidence one-shot), not per process. Keep a process-wide latch only as the sticky operator signal (see F2). Required differential: two distinct booking-error keys in one process \u2192 two `SettlementBookingTerminal` evidence records, two releases.\n\n**F2 \u2014 REQUIRED (either/or): the proposal's operator-health transition was not delivered.**\n`settlement_booking_terminal_latched` has zero consumers outside its own gate \u2014 no operator-health surface wiring exists, so ops-status renders nominal while a position was terminally unbookable. The proposal named \"publish operator-health degraded reason settlement_booking_terminal\" as a constraint; the implementation substituted a `log::error!`. Acceptable resolutions, pick one: (a) wire the latch into the live operator-health surface as a producer snapshot if a cheap seam exists; or (b) de-claim in the PR body (state plainly: operator visibility = ERROR log line + durable evidence only; no health-surface transition) and the follow-up goes to the #1179 ledger \u2014 the same ruling shape as #1229 R-C. The body as written must not claim a health transition that does not exist.\n\n**Verified good at this head (each personally re-read/traced):**\n- Items 1/2 unchanged since prior verification: pool declaration inert beyond settlement currency (all `capital_pools` consumers filter on `enforce_submit_admission` and/or `prediction_market_binary` \u2014 traced individually); validator consumes the single owning predicate with a production-root differential.\n- G1 fixed: `record_entry_skip_once` \u2192 `Result<bool>`; the submit-skip WARN keys on the same evidence dedupe.\n- G2 fixed and class closed: blocked-path WARN on reason-set change; one INFO on blocked\u2192unblocked transition; full field dump `debug!` on both branches; submit-success INFO is event-driven, exits out of entry-class scope by prior ruling.\n- Recovery mirror: restart with an open cache position whose settlement key carries a prior booking-error applies the same terminal release (and on the restart path the fresh process means evidence + ERROR are written).\n- New `SettlementBookingTerminal` lifecycle variant; NT orderbook module-level filter at the correct NT surface; runtime-literal audit updated; boundary-exemption re-point #874\u2192#1179 is mechanical (open-issue fence) with the verifier fixture aligned.\n- Flipped harness expectations match approved rider (a): Managed\u2192Flat asserts with latch checks, listed in the body with rationale.\n\n**Process:** full local test verification (strategy module + archetype + live_node_config scopes) runs at the F1-fixed head \u2014 no point verifying a head that must change. Post-review pushes supersede this round.\n",
      "createdAt": "2026-07-10T13:04:22Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-10T13:04:22Z",
      "author": {
        "login": "seungpyoson"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "IC_kwDOR7A3_s8AAAABJjMSVA",
      "body": "## Owner review \u2014 round 2: both round-1 findings FIXED, verified by execution. Clean.\n\n**Pinned head:** `ddc3efe980e1dde85a6bf0234739fa9dca67ccd5` (round 1 = comment 4935595786 at `f2d1bcb1d`).\n\n**F1 (process-wide latch silenced 2nd+ terminal evidence) \u2014 FIXED, differential verified both ways by me.**\nDelta since round 1 is exactly the strategy file + harness (+94/\u22124; items 1/2/4 byte-identical \u2014 zero drift). The lifecycle evidence + ERROR now dedupe per settlement key via `settlement_booking_terminal_evidence_keys` (one-shot `BTreeSet::insert`), the process-wide latch survives only as the sticky signal, and the recovery mirror threads the key through.\n- **Green:** my run at the exact head \u2014 **678 tests run, 678 passed** across the affected scopes (settlement/booking, entry-skip, strategy module, archetype validation, live-node config), including the new two-key differential.\n- **Red:** my run with only the strategy file reverted to the round-1 head \u2014 the differential **fails** with exactly the round-1 defect signature (second position's `SettlementBookingTerminal` record missing). The differential is genuine.\n\n**F2 (undelivered operator-health transition) \u2014 resolved via lane (b), verified.** The PR body now states plainly that no health-surface transition ships (visibility = per-key ERROR line + durable booking-error + `SettlementBookingTerminal` lifecycle evidence; no operator-ack mechanism), and the follow-up is now actually ledgered \u2014 #1179 follow-up bundle item (6), including the enforcement-activation rider from round-1 note (c).\n\nRound-1 verified items carry over unchanged (pool declaration inert beyond settlement currency; validator on the single owning predicate with production-root differential; entry-path log class closed; recovery mirror; harness flips per approved rider).\n\nFrom my side this head is clean. Remaining process: un-draft (first full-CI run \u2014 DRAFT-DEFAULT means heavy lanes have not run yet), sp-reviewer approval, queue \u2014 owner's. Deploy rider stands: this PR ships a `config/root.toml` change, so the v0.1.12 deploy is binary + config with on-box regeneration.\n",
