      "id": "IC_kwDOR7A3_s8AAAABJjNpnQ",
      "body": "Round 1 addressed at ddc3efe980e1dde85a6bf0234739fa9dca67ccd5.\n\nF1: terminal lifecycle evidence and ERROR output now dedupe by settlement key through settlement_booking_terminal_evidence_keys. Exposure release still applies on every terminal call, while settlement_booking_terminal_latched remains process-sticky. The two-key differential failed at test-only head dd291cfc14866dc448b981a2bdf00a5c67fed7ff in Rust Probe run 29095463213 with only the first position ID present; the same one named test passed at the PR head in run 29096063983.\n\nF2: selected the documented de-claim path. Operator visibility in this slice is ERROR output plus durable booking-error and terminal lifecycle evidence. There is no operator-health transition or acknowledgement clear path; the PR body now states that explicitly.\n\nLocal exact-head gates: just fmt-check and just source-fence-static passed.\n\nPart of #1179",
      "createdAt": "2026-07-10T13:33:27Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-10T13:33:27Z",
      "author": {
        "login": "seungpyoson"
