    {
      "id": "IC_kwDOR7A3_s8AAAABJjT0FA",
      "body": "## Reviewer round (independent battery) \u2014 REQUEST_CHANGES: one blocking test regression the scoped rounds missed\n\n**Pinned:** current head `9d01ac6111b666659c04e994e2d583778f22a71a` (merge-only refresh; content byte-identical to round-2-verified `ddc3efe98` \u2014 I diffed the full PR diff at both heads against their merge-bases: **zero differing lines**). fmt PASS, source-fence-static PASS at head.\n\n**F1 (BLOCKING, control-verified):** `config_parsing::bolt_v3_archetype_keeps_default_provider_market_exit_shape_permissive` FAILS at head and PASSES at main tip (`a226ca2fb`) \u2014 this PR introduces it. The new settlement-currency load validator fires on that test's pre-existing fixture:\n\n```\nstrategy `strategies/binary_oracle.toml`: settlement currency is not derivable for execution venue\n`HYPERLIQUID` account `POLYMARKET-001`; configure risk.capital_pools with matching venue_id/account_id \u2026\n```\n\nMy affected-scope run at head: **1086/1087** (`test(settlement|booking|entry_skip|binary_oracle|live_node_config|archetype) or binary(platform_config)`). The round-2 verification ran 678/678 on a narrower filter that did not include all of `platform_config` \u2014 this is precisely the standing #1238 K-2 rule: *a validation-domain change must enumerate and re-run every test whose fixtures the new domain judges*, and the lane filter must include every test the change can invalidate. A full-suite run at head would have caught it; the merge queue's full CI will fail on it as-is.\n\n**Fix direction (pick per design intent):** (a) if the validator's domain is correct \u2014 any settleable-archetype strategy must derive its settlement currency \u2014 then the fixture is now invalid by design: add a matching non-enforcing `capital_pools` declaration to that test fixture (and sweep the rest of the suite the same way \u2014 run the FULL suite at the fixed head, not a scope filter, and report the count); or (b) if the intent is narrower applicability (e.g., only configs whose venue/archetype combination can actually open settleable positions), the owning predicate needs that refinement plus a differential for the out-of-domain shape. From the fixture's shape (binary-oracle strategy on a mismatched synthetic venue), (a) looks right, but the design call is the owner's.\n\n**Also verified this round:** merge-only refresh clean (diff-of-diffs empty); the failing `gate` check on the PR is a same-SHA carry-forward provenance chain that bottoms out at a transient `in_progress` state \u2014 not a code signal \u2014 but it will be moot either way: full CI at this head will go genuinely red on F1 until fixed.\n",
      "createdAt": "2026-07-10T13:44:37Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-10T13:44:55Z",
      "author": {
        "login": "seungpyoson"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "IC_kwDOR7A3_s8AAAABJjbKVg",
      "body": "## Owner adjudication \u2014 external round (Claude / Grok / GLM / Kimi) + parallel-session CI finding\n\n**Pinned head:** `ddc3efe98` (current tip `9d01ac611` = merge-only refresh, PR-file diff empty \u2014 verified). Verdicts: Claude REQUEST CHANGES (1 blocker), Grok no-blockers (1 suggestion), GLM no-blockers (3 low), Kimi no-blockers (2 low). Every disputed claim re-verified by me against source at the pinned head before this adjudication.\n\n**A1 \u2014 the load-bearing safety claim (Claude blocker vs Grok/GLM/Kimi low): mechanism CONFIRMED, my round-2 derivation CORRECTED, release behavior UPHELD as a deliberate design decision.**\n- Confirmed by my own re-read: `record_missing_interval_end_settlement_booking_error` (mod.rs:1299) fires with **no expiry gate** \u2014 exactly Claude's Family 2. The claim \"every booking-error fires at/after interval end\" is false as stated, and that includes my round-2 approval derivation. On the record: the invariant has **two legs \u2014 market-expired \u2228 position-unmanageable-by-construction** (Kimi's formulation).\n- The second leg holds at this head, verified by me: live-entered positions always carry `interval_end_ms` (`runtime_state.rs:235`, pending-lifecycle inheritance), so the ungated path is reachable **only** through recovery with missing/unparseable instrument metadata; such positions have the exit path permanently blocked (`mod.rs:5248`, `EXIT_BLOCK_REASON_POSITION_INTERVAL_UNKNOWN`) and settlement permanently blocked \u2014 holding occupancy manages nothing and reinstates the park-forever class this PR was ordered to remove. Claude's proposed gate (`interval_ended_at(now_ms)`, retain occupancy on unknown-interval) is REJECTED on that ground: it is fail-closed in name but park-forever in behavior, for a position that can never become manageable (lifecycle does not heal \u2014 confirmed against the harness).\n- Claude's future-risk point is legitimate and becomes a REQUIRED pin: if a future change ever makes unknown-interval reachable for a manageable live position, the release becomes a real double-exposure hole. Required: (i) the two-leg invariant stated in the `apply_settlement_booking_terminal_release` doc comment and PR body (replaces the current overclaim); (ii) a boundary-pin test asserting every live-entered/pending-adopted position carries `interval_end_ms` \u2014 the unmanageable leg must not silently widen.\n\n**CP-1 \u2014 BLOCKER (parallel-session, control-verified; Claude's cross-session signal, same mechanism):** `config_parsing::bolt_v3_archetype_keeps_default_provider_market_exit_shape_permissive` FAILS at head, PASSES at main \u2014 the D2 validator fires on a pre-existing fixture (binary-oracle strategy, no pools). #1238 K-2 class recurrence: a validation-domain change invalidates fixture-based tests outside any scope filter; my 678-test filter missed it. Fix: the fixture gains a matching non-enforcing pool (the fixture now represents a config the new invariant correctly rejects), plus a sweep of every fixture-built root config that hosts a binary-oracle strategy, plus **full suite at head** \u2014 no scope filters for validation-domain changes.\n\n**B (Kimi/GLM/Claude convergent) \u2014 cross-restart duplicate `SettlementBookingTerminal` evidence per key: ACCEPTED-BY-DESIGN, document.** In-memory dedupe is process-local; restart with the residual still open re-emits one lifecycle record + ERROR (distinguishable via `raw_reason_text` live vs restart). Bounded at one per key per process lifetime; fail-loud on the right side. Body documents it; no code change. Kimi's recovery-window note (booking errors older than `recovery.max_bytes` window don't rehydrate \u2192 recovered residual parks \u2014 pre-existing dependency) goes to the #1179 ledger.\n\n**C (all four) \u2014 pool-declaration inertness: unanimously verified**, including the two consumers I had not named (transport client keys, validate/capital non-enforcing branch). Item 1 stands.\n\n**D (flips):** Grok/GLM/Kimi justify all six; Claude contests the two unknown-interval flips \u2014 resolved by the A1 ruling above (they encode the second leg, which is now to be stated, not implied).\n\n**LOW-C (GLM) \u2014 `settlement_booking_terminal_latched` is write-only in production (verified: 3 write sites, zero production readers): REQUIRED cleanup.** Remove the field; re-anchor the six test assertions on `settlement_booking_terminal_evidence_keys` non-emptiness. A write-only bool masquerading as a signal is the built-but-unwired pattern in miniature; ledger item (6) already owns the future health wiring.\n\n**F3 (Claude) \u2014 deploy sharpening: CONFIRMED.** v0.1.12 binary against the old on-box `root.toml` REFUSES BOOT (D2 working as designed). Deploy ships config with binary; body wording sharpened.\n\n**Process lesson, on the record (Claude's articulation, adopted):** suite-green plus a red-proof verifies the mechanism a differential targets; it cannot detect an invariant the same diff deleted, because the flipped tests assert the new behavior. Flipped expectations get adversarial review as first-class findings, not rider compliance checks.\n\n**Punch list (one round):** CP-1 fixture + sweep + full suite at head; two-leg invariant wording (doc + body); boundary-pin test; latch removal; body notes (restart duplicate accepted; deploy refuse-boot). A1 design ruling needs no code change beyond the wording, pin, and latch items.\n",
